          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first to go out (play all cards) each round. Lowest cumulative penalty points after 5 rounds wins the pot.',
          gameplay: '5 rounds total, all dealing 10 cards. Each round has specific contract for initial meld: Round 1: 2 sets of 3; Round 2: 1 set of 3 + 1 run of 4; Round 3: 2 runs of 4; Round 4: 3 sets of 3; Round 5: 1 run of 3 + 1 run of 7. Turn: Draw (take discard top OR push discard+stock card to left player and take next stock card), meld (must meet contract for first meld), discard. Sets: 3-4 cards same rank (max 4 since 2 decks, no duplicate suits in set). Runs: 3+ same suit sequence, Ace high or low (not both). Wild cards (2s/jokers) substitute any card. Can lay off on any meld after meeting contract. Can replace wild cards with natural cards from hand (wild must be used immediately in new meld). Go out by melding/discarding all cards.',
          keyRules: [
            'All 5 rounds deal 10 cards each',
            'Individual play - no partnerships',
            'Must meet contract before any other melding',
            'Draw: take discard OR push discard+stock to left and take next stock',
            'Sets: 3-4 cards same rank, no duplicate suits',
            'Runs: 3+ consecutive same suit, Ace high or low',
            '2s and jokers are wild',
            'Round 5 contract: run of 3 + run of 7 (different from Push)',
            'Can replace wilds with naturals (wild must be reused immediately)',
            'Lowest cumulative score after 5 rounds wins pot',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Focus on meeting the contract requirement first. Hold wild cards for flexibility. Watch what cards opponents are collecting.',
          intermediate: "Plan ahead for upcoming contracts. Use the 'push' mechanic strategically - forcing cards on opponents can disrupt their plans. Replace wild cards when beneficial to free them for other melds.",
          advanced: "Track discards and pushes to deduce opponent hands. Time your go-out to maximize opponent penalties. In gambling version, manage risk based on pot size and your position. Round 5's run of 7 is difficult - prepare early.",
          tips: [
            'Save wild cards for difficult contracts',
            'The push mechanic can be used defensively to give opponents unwanted cards',
            "Round 5's run of 7 requires early preparation",
            'Replacing a wild card can enable a new meld',
            'Going out quickly may be better than perfect melds',
            'Watch opponent discards for clues about their contracts',
          ],
